{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>To love HaShem, etc.</b> This statement is attached to what is above it, where He said ״לְמַעַן תִּחְיֶה אַתָּה וְזַרְעֶךָ״, and He concluded by saying ״לְאַהֲבָה״ etc. — meaning, that the essence of the desire for life is to love HaShem, to hearken to His voice, etc., and He gave the reason ״כִּי הוּא חַיֶּיךָ״ — for what does a person have of life if not the will of the Blessed One, for doing His will is what surrounds a person so that he may cleave to his Maker, as He said ״וּלְדָבְקָה בוֹ״, and this itself is the very essence of life in this world and length of days for the World to Come, and this is what He said ״וְאֹרֶךְ יָמֶיךָ״." "And His saying <b>to dwell upon, etc.</b> — as if He said וְלָשֶׁבֶת (and to dwell), etc. And this matter too is part of the attainment of perfection, for dwelling in the Land is a mitzvah that encompasses the entire Torah. Go and learn from the statement of our Sages of blessed memory (Ketubot 111a) that whoever walks in it four cubits has a share in the World to Come, all of which is life." "<b>Conclusion of the portion of Nitzavim</b>"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:20:28.633899164Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}